course: dictionary
lesson: 3156
title: Emergency: when help is needed now
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An emergency is a sudden, dangerous situation where help is needed quickly. Use the words around it to work out its meaning. «In an emergency, stay calm and get safe.» This tells you that an emergency is a time when you must act fast and carefully, so it must be a situation that needs help now.
explain: «Heat exhaustion can turn into heatstroke, a medical emergency.» The word medical is a clue: it is about health. Try your meaning in the sentence: "heatstroke, a sudden dangerous health problem that needs help quickly" still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Emergency can also be an adjective, a word that describes a noun. «Emergency exit» is a door you use when there is danger, such as a fire. «Emergency services» are the people who come to help in a dangerous situation. Learn these phrases together, because the word often appears inside them.
explain: «In an emergency there is no time to chat: if there is a fire, you get out and call the emergency number.» This is the most important lesson. In an emergency, act first and talk later. Know your address and your family's plan before an emergency happens.
fact: An emergency is a sudden, dangerous situation where help is needed quickly.
fact: Examples of emergencies are a fire, a bad accident, or someone who cannot breathe.
fact: As a noun, the plural is emergencies. As an adjective, it describes things such as an emergency exit.
fact: In an emergency, stay calm, get safe, and call the emergency number.
fact: Emergency numbers differ by country: 911 (USA, Canada), 999 or 112 (UK, Ireland), 000 (Australia), 111 (New Zealand). Say your address and what happened, then listen.
exercise: «In an emergency, stay calm and get safe.» What should you do in an emergency? | *Stay calm and get safe | Hide under the table | Ask a bot what to do | Panic and run in circles
exercise: «An emergency exit» is a door. What does emergency tell you about when it is used? | *When there is danger, such as a fire | When it is time for lunch | When it is raining | When the shop is closed
exercise: «A swallowed button battery can burn through the throat in about two hours, so it is always an emergency.» Why is it an emergency? | *It is dangerous and needs help quickly | It means the battery is new | It is a fun game | It is a kind of food
test: Which word means a sudden dangerous situation where help is needed quickly? | Puzzle | Holiday | *Emergency | Lullaby
test: «Heat exhaustion can turn into heatstroke, a medical emergency.» What is a medical emergency? | A problem with food that tastes bad | A game played in the park | *A health problem that needs help quickly | A type of weather
exam: Which of these is an emergency number in the UK? | 000 | 911 | *999 | 111
